WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.434
-Leslie, thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.601
-Thank you.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:05.667
-We just had your daughter,
Maude Apatow,

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.133
on the show recently.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:10.200
And, man, she's just crushing
it, crushing it, crushing it.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.300
You know I love the family.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.167
And Iris is great in
"The Bubble," too.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.934
-Thank you.
-But you have great kids.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.300
-Thank you!
-You've got to be very proud.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.934
-I am so proud.
They're good girls.

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:20.200
-They really are.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.701
They're just good people
and funny and great actors.

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:25.067
Oh, my gosh.
-I know.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.467
You know, I don't know if
you feel like this,

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:30.434
but as a parent,
when you're given these

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.968
two beautiful little babies,
you don't want to, like,

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.133
ruin them with bad parenting.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.334
-Of course.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:41.367
-And so it's a lot of pressure
on us parents.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:45.667
And, yeah, I feel like --
Looking at them now,

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.300
I feel like, "Okay, well,
maybe I didn't ruin them.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.667
Maybe they're okay."

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.000
-You beyond did not.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.868
You beyond did not.
You should be very, very proud.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.033
They're awesome.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.033
-They're, like,
good, kind-hearted people.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.033
-Funny, funny.
-But we don't want to jinx it.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.801
-No. No, no one's -- And that's
not even real wood at all,

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.200
so it doesn't matter
what you're doing.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.734
Watch someone comes out
from underneath.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.167
"Oh, hi."

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:11.200
Judd Apatow is your husband.
Very funny human being.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.000
And you guys have been married
for 25 years?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.434
-25 years in June.
-Is that right?

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:20.167
-Wow.
-Isn't that crazy?

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.167
-It is crazy.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.601
Do you celebrate 25?

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:26.434
-So, 25 -- Well, we are
planning on having party.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.834
We got married
by ourselves in Hawaii --

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.901
just the two of us and
a banjo player and a minister.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:32.934
And --

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:35.300
-Fun.
-It kind of was fun.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.734
It was low-pressure.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:40.634
And then we promised each other
that we would have a party

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.968
with friends and family at
like our five-year anniversary.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.067
-Cool.
-We didn't.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.467
-Oh.
-So then we said 10-year.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.734
And then we forgot.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:50.467
And then 15 and 20,
we didn't do it.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.601
I think we're, like,

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:55.033
afraid that people
won't come to our party.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.033
-What?

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.901
-I think that's, like -- Yeah.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.334
-You guys, would you go?

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:00.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.267
The whole audience -- If you
invite the whole audience --

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.367
Yeah.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.868
-Okay. That'd be fun.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.634
-You have to have a party.
-You think?

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.701
-Yeah, you're
the most fun family.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.000
-Okay.
-Yeah, you're great.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.033
-I'm gonna work on it.
-Have a rager.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.467
-We won't do it.
We're not gonna do it.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.567
-Who care -- If no one shows up,
it's funnier.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.734
-You think? Oh, really?
-Yes.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:19.934
Wouldn't that be great
if no one showed up?

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.133
-That would be so bad.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.501
-No, that's another story that

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:23.701
you come on the show
and talk to me about --

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.801
-Okay, okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.467
Here's a photo of you guys,
by the way,

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.234
on your wedding day,
you and Judd.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.534
-Okay, so this -- Wait.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.467
On our wedding day, Judd,

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.601
who I'd only known
with a beard --

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:38.934
-Me too.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.200
-I mean, I didn't date Judd
or anything, but yeah.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.667
-He was a cute, like,
mountain-man-looking Judd.

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:48.434
And on our wedding day,
he decided to shave his beard

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.434
and showed up to our
wedding clean-shaven.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.033
And it really scared me,

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:57.367
because I didn't know what he
looked like without it.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:03:00.501
And my kids, when they were
little, he would, like,

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.968
suddenly shave his beard,

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:05.901
and they would start shaking and
crying and be like, "No!"

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:08.901
And, okay, so, this is --
He's so cute,

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.200
but, like, if you didn't know
what was under there --

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.300
Well, look.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.501
Can you go close?
-Oh.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:18.501
-But look at his teeth.
It's like...

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.100
-What do you mean?
He has good teeth.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.734
I've also never really seen
a pose like this.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.000
What's happening?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.767
-Oh, and look at his --
-Like, are you falling?

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:32.701
Was he -- Did you know him
before this photo was taken?

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.734
Or did he grab you and go like,

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:38.100
"You're gorgeous,
I've got to marry you"?

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.534
-What is he doing?
-It's a very interesting pose.

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:41.567
I've never seen that
move before.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:42.701
But he went for it.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:46.033
-I feel like
we should be scared for me.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.734
-Next time you guys are both
on the show together,

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:51.567
I want to re-create
the pose and the arm hold.

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:52.868
That's great.

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:54.834
I want to talk about
"The Bubble"

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.334
because it's very funny.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:04:00.501
And it's about the pandemic and
actors and a big action movie.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.367
But last time
you were on our show,

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.534
we talked about how
you love to roller-skate.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:05.601
And then I see the movie,

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.067
and you're roller-skating
in the movie.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.234
And I go -- It had to be you.
You put that in there, right?

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:10.334
-Well, I -- Yeah.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.167
I was having so much fun
roller-skating,

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.400
and then I thought, "Oh, well,

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.434
my character should know how to
roller-skate."

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.834
-Of course.
-That would be fun.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:19.901
And then -- Yeah.
So, it was super-fun.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:24.767
But I did have the --
I was roller-skating

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:28.868
while we were shooting, and I --

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:33.567
It was, like, a windy day,
and I was doing, like, a turn.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:37.000
And the wind,
like, whipped me around.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.834
And I fell down on
my chin and cut my chin open.

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:43.968
And I had to be rushed
to the hospital.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.634
There's blood everywhere.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:51.701
And the doctor had to, like,
scrape rocks out of my inside

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.300
of a deep cut.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.400
It was so gross.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.267
And then, like,
they had to cauterize it,

00:04:56.267 --> 00:05:00.667
which means burning it shut,
and then stitched it up.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:04.667
-Wait. Who was your doctor?
Like, Pa Ingalls?

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.968
Corduroys.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.467
Do you remember that episode?
-Yes.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.300
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.400
-Dude, that was
a crazy episode, man.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.868
Ma Ingalls --

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.300
It was that awful.
It was unbelievable.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.033
I'll never forget that episode.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.934
But you actually
brought a photo.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:21.267
This is real.
There's you with your chin.

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:22.400
-Yes.
-It's very bloody.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.033
It looks --
This is after they kind of

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.167
cleaned it up a little bit.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.901
But, yeah,
it was very deep and gross.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:29.968
-So, after this, you're like --

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.601
You kind of got scared
to roller-skate.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:33.701
-So then I didn't roller-skate
again for a year

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:36.601
because I was so traumatized.

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:39.567
And then I thought, "Well,
I'm not going to let something

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:42.601
like that stop me from doing
something I love."

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:44.033
-That's right. See?

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.167
Confront your fears.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.567
"Confront your fears" is
the theme of our show tonight.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:52.400
-Okay, so,
I got back up on the horse.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:56.067
And I made
you and The Roots a video.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.300
-Yep, here's the video.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.167
Here's Leslie Mann returning
to roller skating.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:01.634
Roots, watch this.

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.200
-♪ You better come out with ♪

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.133
♪ Your hands up,
we got you surrounded ♪

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:07.234
♪ I'm in the back,
changing my outfit ♪

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:09.234
♪ He said "Blink,"
we gonna send the hounds in ♪

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.334
♪ I said, "Wait,
'cause here I come" ♪

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.200
♪ Here I come, here I come ♪

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.400
♪ You boys get ready,
'cause here I come ♪

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.367
♪ Here I come, here I come ♪

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:20.167
♪ He said, "Yeah, you better
come out with your hands up ♪

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:21.701
♪ We got you surrounded" ♪

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:23.534
-"I'm in the back --" Come on!
♪♪

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.133
The greatest!

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:29.934
I love you. Look at you.
-Right?

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:31.801
-The down move was the best one.
-I know.

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:32.901
-It's so cool.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:36.467
-It's so weird
that I can do that.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:37.868
-I'm so happy that you --

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:39.300
Thank you for shooting
that video for us.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.734
-Oh, you're welcome.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.934
-Now, we're here to talk about
the film "The Bubble," okay?

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:46.701
Written and directed by
your husband, Judd Apatow.

00:06:46.701 --> 00:06:49.033
Can you set up what it's about?
-Sure, sure, yeah.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:56.767
So, "The Bubble" is a hilarious,
laugh-out-loud Netflix comedy

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:59.834
which follows a group of
narcissistic actors

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:02.834
stuck inside a pandemic bubble
at a luxury hotel

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:07.634
attempting to complete a sequel
to an action franchise film

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.534
about flying dinosaurs called

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:12.601
"Cliff Beasts 6:
The Battle for Everest,

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:14.901
Memories of a Requiem."

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:18.033
-That sounds great,
but I just --

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:20.300
-Yeah.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.968
-Were you just reading
the plot description or --

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:24.767
I mean, can --
-No. Oh, no, no, no.

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:26.200
No!

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.934
-Can you tell us who else --
Tell who else is in the film.

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:36.634
-Okay. So, it's a
star-studded cast that includes

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:39.634
David Duchovny...

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:41.634
Fred Armisen...

00:07:43.834 --> 00:07:48.167
Keegan-Michael Key, Iris Apatow,
Karen Gillan, Pedro Pascal,

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:53.434
Maria Bakalova, and Leslie Mann
as Lauren Van Chance.

00:07:53.434 --> 00:07:56.200
in the riotous romp --

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.868
-Introducing your...

00:07:58.868 --> 00:08:02.167
-I would --
That's KNBC San Diego

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:04.667
calls "the lockdown comedy
we've all been waiting for."

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:05.734
We have a clip.

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.634
-No, no.
Now I say, "We have a clip."

00:08:07.634 --> 00:08:10.200
That's -- I'm the one who
normally throws to the clip.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.367
-Oh, okay.
-Yeah.

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:13.968
Here's Leslie Mann in
"The Bubble."

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.934
Take a look at this.

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:17.934
Oh, no.

00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:20.400
That sounds like a baby crying
for its mama.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.400
-Whoa!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.267
-That ain't no baby!

00:08:26.367 --> 00:08:27.968
-Oh, my God!
What are we going to do?!

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:32.100
-Oh!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.434
-[ Screaming ]

00:08:33.434 --> 00:08:34.934
-Somebody help him!

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:36.501
-Help him!

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.267
Hang in there!

00:08:41.267 --> 00:08:43.701
-How does he fly?
He has no feathers.

00:08:43.701 --> 00:08:46.000
-Well, somebody taught him
how to fly.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.667
-Please stop!

00:08:48.667 --> 00:08:49.968
It's okay! I got him!

00:08:49.968 --> 00:08:51.868
-[ Screaming ]

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:53.234
-Aah!

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:55.067
-[ Screaming ]

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.534
-Yaah!

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:58.167
[ Screaming continues ]

00:08:58.167 --> 00:08:59.734
-Alright. Cut.

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:04.133
-"The Bubble."
Leslie Mann, everybody!

